# Aarogya Localization Rules

## Supported Languages

Aarogya must support:

1. English
2. Hindi

Hindi must use proper Devanagari script.

Do not use Hinglish for Hindi UI.

Example:

Correct:

"संभावित गिरने की घटना का पता चला"

Incorrect:

"Possible fall detect hua"

## No Hard Coded User Text

Do not hard code user facing strings directly inside:

• Widgets
• Business logic
• Services
• State classes
• Error handlers

Use localization keys.

## Localization Structure

Every user facing English string should have a corresponding Hindi translation.

Example:

health_status
English:
"Health Status"

Hindi:
"स्वास्थ्य स्थिति"

## Emergency Translation

Emergency messages must remain concise.

English:

"Possible fall detected."

Hindi:

"संभावित गिरने की घटना का पता चला।"

English:

"Connectivity unavailable."

Hindi:

"कनेक्टिविटी उपलब्ध नहीं है।"

## Technical Terms

Do not translate:

• Code identifiers
• Database field names
• API fields
• Enum identifiers
• File names
• Internal model names

User facing technical terms should use understandable Hindi where appropriate.

## Language Switching

Changing language must not:

• Reset application state
• Delete data
• Exit Disaster Mode
• Exit Survival Mode
• Cancel emergency monitoring
• Delete emergency events

If the user changes language during an emergency, the active emergency state must continue.

## Layout Testing

Hindi text can occupy different amounts of space.

Test:

• Buttons
• Cards
• Navigation
• Alerts
• Dialogs
• Long instructions
• Emergency screens

Never assume English text width.

## Accessibility

Hindi and English text must maintain:

• Readability
• Adequate font size
• Adequate contrast
• Proper line spacing

Do not solve Hindi overflow by making the font extremely small.
